📘 README – API Express.js + Sequelize
📌 Description

Cette API permet la gestion d’utilisateurs, de profils, d’intérêts, d’activités, de réservations et de conversations avec messagerie.
Elle est construite avec Express.js et Sequelize (ORM SQL).

🚀 Technologies

Node.js (Express.js)

Sequelize + PostgreSQL (ou MySQL, selon besoin)

JWT (authentification)

bcrypt (hashage des mots de passe)

Modèles et Relations avec Types
USER
Champ	Type Sequelize	Options
id	INTEGER	PK, autoIncrement
email	STRING	unique, allowNull: false
password	STRING	allowNull: false
role	ENUM('user','admin')	defaultValue: 'user'
actif	BOOLEAN	defaultValue: true

Relations :

User ➝ 1-1 ➝ Profile

User ➝ N-N ➝ Reservation (via UserReservation)

User ➝ 1-N ➝ Message

PROFILE
Champ	Type Sequelize	Options
id	INTEGER	PK, autoIncrement
user_id	INTEGER	FK(User.id), unique, allowNull: false
nom	STRING	allowNull: false
prenom	STRING	allowNull: false
age	INTEGER	allowNull: true
biographie	TEXT	allowNull: true
pays	STRING	allowNull: true
ville	STRING	allowNull: true
img_url	STRING	allowNull: true

Relations :

Profile ➝ belongsTo User

Profile ➝ N-N ➝ Interet (via ProfileInteret)

INTERET
Champ	Type Sequelize	Options
id	INTEGER	PK, autoIncrement
name	STRING	unique, allowNull: false
icon	STRING	allowNull: true
actif	BOOLEAN	defaultValue: true

Relations :

Interet ➝ N-N ➝ Profile

RESERVATION
Champ	Type Sequelize	Options
id	INTEGER	PK, autoIncrement
status	ENUM('pending','accepted','rejected')	defaultValue: 'pending'
conversation_id	INTEGER	FK(Conversation.id), allowNull: true

Relations :

Reservation ➝ N-N ➝ User (via UserReservation)

Reservation ➝ 1-N ➝ Activity

Reservation ➝ belongsTo Conversation

ACTIVITY
Champ	Type Sequelize	Options
id	INTEGER	PK, autoIncrement
title	STRING	allowNull: false
prix	DECIMAL(10,2)	allowNull: false
start_date	DATE	allowNull: false
end_date	DATE	allowNull: false
reservation_id	INTEGER	FK(Reservation.id), allowNull: false

Relations :

Activity ➝ belongsTo Reservation

CONVERSATION
Champ	Type Sequelize	Options
id	INTEGER	PK, autoIncrement
user1_id	INTEGER	FK(User.id), allowNull: false
user2_id	INTEGER	FK(User.id), allowNull: false

Relations :

Conversation ➝ 1-N ➝ Message

Conversation ➝ 1-1 ➝ Reservation

MESSAGE
Champ	Type Sequelize	Options
id	INTEGER	PK, autoIncrement
user_id	INTEGER	FK(User.id), allowNull: false
conversation_id	INTEGER	FK(Conversation.id), allowNull: false
content	TEXT	allowNull: false
read	BOOLEAN	defaultValue: false
attachement	STRING	allowNull: true

Relations :

Message ➝ belongsTo User

Message ➝ belongsTo Conversation

USER_RESERVATION (table pivot)
Champ	Type Sequelize	Options
user_id	INTEGER	FK(User.id)
reservation_id	INTEGER	FK(Reservation.id)

Relations :

User ↔ Reservation (N-N)

PROFILE_INTERET (table pivot)
Champ	Type Sequelize	Options
profile_id	INTEGER	FK(Profile.id)
interet_id	INTEGER	FK(Interet.id)

Relations :

Profile ↔ Interet (N-N)


🔗 Diagramme simplifié des relations
User ─── 1:1 ─── Profile
User ─── N:N ─── Reservation (via UserReservation)
Profile ─── N:N ─── Interet
Reservation ─── 1:N ─── Activity
Reservation ─── 1:1 ─── Conversation
Conversation ─── 1:N ─── Message
User ─── 1:N ─── Message